# ============================================================================
#  CTN 2026 — Docker build context exclusions
# ============================================================================
#  This file is a SECURITY BOUNDARY, not an optimisation.
#
#  Rule 5.6: never share competition API keys beyond your team.
#  COPYing .env into the image bakes the key into an image layer, readable by
#  anyone who can run `docker save` or `docker history`.
#
#  Separately: state/ and logs/ are runtime data. They must live on volumes and
#  must never enter the image.
# ============================================================================

# ---- Secrets: highest priority, never enter the image ----------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
secrets/
credentials/
credentials*.json
*_secret*
*_token.txt

# ---- Runtime state and logs: must go through volumes ----------------------
state/
logs/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3*
checkpoint*
*.jsonl
*.log

# ---- Competition materials (Rule 5.2) -------------------------------------
materials/
briefings/
official/
*.pdf
discord-export*
screenshots/

# ---- Version control and local environments ------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

.conda/
envs/
venv/
.venv/
environment.lock.yml

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ---- Editors / operating systems -----------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
scratch/
tmp/
*.local.*
local_*

# ---- Docs and previews (not needed at runtime; keeps the image small) -----
docs/
*.html
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
README.md
agent.md
